00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.294
This video demonstrates how to perform the fundal reflex test.

2
00:00:04.294 --> 00:00:07.300
Start with hand hygiene and introduce yourself.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:13.741
Confirm the identity of the baby, explain the examination and gain consent to perform it.

4
00:00:13.741 --> 00:00:20.612
The baby should be held securely and comfortably either on the lap or over a shoulder.

5
00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:23.618
It's important for them to feel safe.

6
00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:28.341
Start by asking if there are any concerns about general development,

7
00:00:28.341 --> 00:00:33.065
eyesight or the appearance of the eyes, then make some observations.

8
00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:36.500
Get a sense of the baby's general and

9
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.992
visual development by looking at the way they move, their tone and posture and

10
00:00:39.992 --> 00:00:40.740
how well they

11
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.684
can fix on your face and eyes.

12
00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:45.460
Move your head from side to side, increase your distance

13
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.815
and make silent smiles.

14
00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:51.220
Take note of how steady fixation is, if they respond to your silent

15
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.888
smile and the distance at which they lose fixation.

16
00:00:53.888 --> 00:00:56.260
At the same time look for any signs

17
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.733
of wobbly eyes, squint, red eye or white pupil.

18
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:02.820
Then prepare the arc light by selecting the

19
00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.632
the brightest light setting with three clicks.

20
00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:07.220
Make sure the lens rack is at the top where

21
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.673
there is no lens power in the sighthole.

22
00:01:09.673 --> 00:01:12.127
Examination room needs to be quiet and dim.

23
00:01:12.127 --> 00:01:12.740
Most babies

24
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.793
will naturally look at a light.

25
00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:18.900
Get the sighthole close to your eye and at arm's length observe

26
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.225
the fungal reflex in both eyes at the same time.

27
00:01:22.225 --> 00:01:24.220
Compare the brightness and colour between

28
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.215
the two eyes.

29
00:01:25.215 --> 00:01:29.860
Look for any dark patches in the reflex or complete absence of the reflex.

30
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.949
trying to note the position of the corneal reflections.

31
00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:36.220
The appearance will vary depending

32
00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.822
on your distance from the baby and the angle of examination.

33
00:01:39.822 --> 00:01:41.460
In a normal examination there

34
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.199
should be no overall difference in the brightness and colour between the two eyes

35
00:01:45.199 --> 00:01:46.000
with the corneal

36
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.436
reflections appearing central.

37
00:01:47.436 --> 00:01:52.700
This is a normal fundal reflex test of a white baby.

38
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.028
In non-white babies the colour of the fundal reflex is different.

39
00:01:56.028 --> 00:01:57.540
The reflex tends to be

40
00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.240
a paler with yellow, white, and even blue the main reflect in colors.

41
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.585
This is what the normal examination of a black baby looks like, and is

42
00:02:05.585 --> 00:02:06.780
why this test is increasingly

43
00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:12.620
called the fundal reflex test, rather than the misleading red reflex test.

44
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.200
Abnormal findings are when there is a persistent overall color or brightness difference between

45
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:23.460
the two eyes, a displaced corneal reflection, a dark patch present within the reflex of one

46
00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.220
or both eyes, or a completely absent reflex.

47
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.380
To summarize, a normal examination is when there is no overall difference in the brightness

48
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:38.380
and colour between the two eyes, with central corneal reflections.

49
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.580
An abnormal fungal reflex is when there is a difference in the brightness and colour

50
00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:48.060
between the two eyes, a displaced corneal reflection, a dark patch present within the

51
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.017
reflex of one or both eyes, or a completely absent reflex.

52
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:55.100
An abnormal

53
00:02:55.100 --> 00:03:01.660
fundal reflex test can indicate the presence of cataract, retublastoma, corneal

54
00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:07.900
scar, squint, refractive error, or a structural abnormality such as coloboa.

55
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.536
These all require further assessment by a specialist.

56
00:03:11.536 --> 00:03:12.900
After the examination

57
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.020
repeat hand hygiene, thank the parent or care and document and explain your

58
00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:17.382
findings.

59
00:03:17.382 --> 00:03:20.644
Agree a clear plan for further assessment if needed.

60
